According to the documented rule for conformance.kernel.recovery, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text' [a84bcb8e1134b8b4]. In the input, the code fence contains the sentence S and the JSON object A. Since the fence holds an object, A is the scored object. In the rewritten text, the JSON object A is removed from inside the code fence, leaving only the sentence S. The fence no longer holds an object, and there are no top-level objects outside the fence (only the sentence S). Thus the recovered object moves from {"a": 1} to NO_OBJECT.